= Results <sec:validation>

What was run and what came out of it. Observations belong here; what they mean
is @sec:discussion.

== Frequency shift as a quality proxy <sec:proxy-validation>

Before the routine's results are worth anything, the number it optimizes has to
be worth something. Constant-current images of three apexes on partially
oxidized Cu(110), acquired in separate sessions and independent of the
conditioning runs, are the evidence that $Delta f$ tracks the images an
operator would judge by.

== Unattended conditioning runs <sec:hardware-results>

Two runs started from blunt tips and reached the sharp bounds within seven
minutes. One passed the stability test; the other returned to pulsing on its
own. The routine has also run safely for over an hour on tips that never
reached the bounds, which is its own kind of result.

Cycles to a sharp tip, time to convergence, and how often a run ended in each
outcome.

== Verification against the mock controller <sec:mock-results>

The mock controller exercised the paths that are hard to provoke on real
hardware, and the two protocol boundaries of @sec:interface and @sec:analyzers
were tested against real servers rather than stubs.

Which parts of the current implementation have hardware evidence behind them
and which have only this is stated plainly, since the distinction matters for
everything claimed in @sec:discussion.
